    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_2a2b15ddfd22f855b06b3b1b2e76ab8a4e61d966746fba1ca685868970b10e67",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Across the exact delta-boundary trap and the Berry-Keating specialization, embedded localization is an interference condition rather than generic discreteness: the coupling magnitude must be tuned and its sign selects the phase crossings where endpoint amplitudes cancel. In the trap detuning opens leakage and turns bound states into resonances; in the Berry-Keating case inverse-energy corrections prevent exact cancellation, so the smooth Riemann locations are likewise described more appropriately as resonances.",
