    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_2b7681cc22260820931df89a4629b709ae6b648b51e610003ca976b79000e162",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source builds a conditional counting-to-Jost pipeline: smooth xp area gives the baseline density, curved boundary displacement encodes a fluctuation correction, an imposed operator lift integrates that correction into phases of dual boundary transforms, and a Cauchy projection reduces the Jost determinant to the resulting total phase. A truncated Riemann-Siegel sum then supplies an approximate fluctuation phase whose low-zero agreement is inherited from that approximation.",
