    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_58c748b734c9eb0f52ccf466dd016f6e53514b38d9d58c6cbcbc23a841e257fe",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source lifts exchange symmetry through successive representations: cosine or sine Fourier duality selects a half-line parity/domain choice, Mellin transformation records it as the even or odd completed-L-function gamma phase, and fluctuation constraints add a counting phase to the dual boundary amplitudes. For the even zeta specialization, their exchange-covariant sum motivates a critical-line amplitude-times-cosine factorization.",
