    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_5cd760107e08bc49566fa37748ea5fe28161751a658c1c3954ed94921493ea63",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Under the imposed exchange symmetry, the deformed exclusion curves encode a fluctuation density through logarithmic boundary displacement; the quantum construction then compresses those two boundary roles into real states coupled by an antisymmetric rank-two interaction, whose projection-and-transfer interpretation glues equal-energy boundary hits into closed allowed trajectories while retaining an open continuum channel.",
