    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b6c2f230f873d2c7f8398f36d99d538f271413f92d2e7417f70a052b990a35c1",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Berry-Keating smoothing replaces the discontinuous Riemann-Siegel cutoff by contour-defined weights and yields an exact dual decomposition ζ(1/2-it)=e^{2iθ(t)}f(t)+f(-t). Turning this identity into the proposed Jost factorization requires two additional gates: real-axis nonvanishing of f so its fluctuation phase is defined and does not supply competing zeros, and upper-half-plane analyticity and decay of the induced total phase so the overlap determinant collapses to the assumed Jost form.",
