    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_f44a12f9eea6b0771f62ed53de58c3a8b8f187cf70f7634bec9e6be86dc85bde",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source tests two non-equivalent routes by which prime information might enter the fluctuation model. The formal critical-line prime sum suggests prime-labelled periodic orbits but fails convergence and finite-winding/sign tests; later, a finite additive Dirichlet sum shares terms and qualitative phase features with a finite multiplicative prime product without equaling it. Together these routes narrow, but do not supply, a classical prime mechanism for the antisymmetric interaction.",
